 ── 26th of August 2026
 + Added modules. Sutff like GIT, NET, TOR, Etc. are all optional modules.
 + Added !modules command to support this feature. 
   You can directly install/remove modules trough the !modules command.
   More modules will hopefully come soon if i'm not lazy
 + Added '!md' alias for accessing !modules easier
 + Added checks for needed packages - If you do not have them installed,
 You will be prompted with a install

 ── 27th of August 2026
 + Added the LINKS Module! 
 + You can now install the LINKS module and do things like:
  > Shorten URLs 
  > Generate passwords
  > Manage your shortened URLs
  > checks if a URL is valid (any)
 ── 4th of September 2026
 + Added Cobalt!
  > Cobalt is a Open-Source Self-Hosted media downloader.
  > You can use it to download videos or music
  > List of supported wbesites: https://pkw.arch-linux.fun/p/k9pba6rfeu
  > (if you don't feel like going to the website, yes youtube is supported)
  > (soundcloud too, and even instagram and tiktok)
  > Cobalt is completely hosted on YOUR machine, Though, the set-up process has been automated.
  > You're welcome!
 + Variables now in Modules! Less bloat in !help, everyone's happy. Help section per module.
  > Example usage: !tor help, !url help, !cobalt help, etc.
